package RenderingChecks

use Libraries.Game.Physics.PhysicsProperties3D
use Libraries.Interface.Item3D

/*
ReportingPhysicsProperties3D is the physics data of a Model2. It works as
PhysicsProperties3D does, and also tells its Model2 whenever physics starts
or stops simulating it, so the Model2 can tell its layer.

Every way a body wakes or falls asleep goes through Simulate: setting a
velocity, applying a force, torque or impulse, requiring simulation, and
the solver putting a group to sleep or waking a body it reaches. Those all
call Simulate on the properties, so replacing that one action catches all
of them.

Attribute: Example

use RenderingChecks.Model2
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Color

// A Model2 uses these properties when its physics is enabled.
Color color
Model2 box
box:LoadBox(1, 1, 1, color:Teal())
box:EnablePhysics(true)
box:Simulate(false)
*/
class ReportingPhysicsProperties3D is PhysicsProperties3D
    /*
    This action starts or stops simulating the body, as PhysicsProperties3D
    does, and tells the body's Model2 if that changed.

    Attribute: Parameter flag True to simulate the body, false to put it to
    sleep.
    */
    action Simulate(boolean flag)
        boolean before = IsSimulated()
        parent:PhysicsProperties3D:Simulate(flag)
        if before not= flag
            Item3D owner = GetItem()
            if owner is Model2
                Model2 model = cast(Model2, owner)
                model:SimulationChanged()
            end
        end
    end
end
